8,Zapotecan Family | SIL Mexico,https://mexico.sil.org/language_culture/zapotec,"Like other Otomanguean languages, most Zapotecan languages are tonal, which means that the pitch with which a word is pronounced is so important that a change in the pitch can change one word into an entirely different one. However, tone is not marked in the practical orthographies (alphabets) because the correct tones of a word can usually be determined by the context.","Zapotec, Yautepec",Otomanguean
9,MUSIC OF THE ISTHMUS OF TEHUANTEPEC OAXACA | Mexican Rarities,https://mexicanrarities.com/archive/mexico/oaxaca/chontales/music-of-the-isthmus-of-tehuantepec-oaxaca/,"March 5, 2025 - Vinyl, LP, Album MUSIC FROM THE ISTHMUS OF TEHUANTEPEC OAXACA. In the hot and dry land of the southern Oaxacan part of the Isthmus of Tehuantepec, various musical traditions have been developed by different ethnic groups: the Zapotecs of the Isthmus, the Huaves or Mareños, the Mixes, the Chontals and the Zoques.","Zapotec, Yautepec",Otomanguean
